    <string name="intro_coach_crowns">Place one crown in each row, column, and colour region; crowns never touch, even diagonally. Tap an empty cell for X, tap again for a crown, and tap once more to clear.</string>
    <string name="intro_coach_binary">Each row and column needs three of each symbol, and no three alike may touch.</string>
    <string name="intro_coach_nonogram">A clue gives the length of a filled run; a 5 fills the whole column.</string>
    <string name="intro_coach_minisudoku">Each row, column, and 2 by 3 box uses digits 1 through 6 once; fill the cell with only one possible digit.</string>
    <string name="intro_coach_sudoku">Each row, column, and 3 by 3 box uses digits 1 through 9 once; fill the cell with only one possible digit.</string>
    <string name="intro_coach_skyscrapers">From each edge, count the buildings you can see; taller buildings hide those behind them.</string>
    <string name="intro_coach_futoshiki">Fill each row and column with 1 to N once. Follow the inequality signs between neighbouring cells.</string>
    <string name="intro_coach_path">Connect each matching numbered pair, filling every cell without crossing or touching another part of the same path.</string>
    <string name="intro_coach_killersudoku">Each row, column, and 3 by 3 box uses digits 1 through 9 once; digits in each dashed cage cannot repeat and must add up to the cage sum.</string>
    <string name="intro_coach_arrows">Tap an arrow with a clear path to the edge to slide it off the board; three blocked taps end the level.</string>
    <string name="intro_coach_coloursort">Tap a tube, then tap another to pour. Matching colours stack, and an empty tube takes any colour. Fill each tube with one colour.</string>
    <string name="intro_coach_mosaic">A number is how many filled cells sit in that cell and its neighbours. Fill or Cross until every clue is true.</string>
    <string name="intro_coach_klondike">Build each foundation up in suit from ace to king. Flip tableau cards, and draw from the stock one at a time.</string>
    <string name="intro_coach_tactics">Tap the piece that mates, then tap the square it moves to. You play the winning side; the opponent does not move in mate in one.</string>
