    <string name="play_rules_title">How to play %1$s</string>
    <string name="play_rules_crowns">Place one crown in each row, column, and colour region. Crowns cannot touch, even diagonally. Tap an empty cell for X, tap again for a crown, and tap once more to clear. Long press to clear a cell.</string>
    <string name="play_rules_binary">Fill each row and column with equal numbers of the two symbols. No three matching symbols may touch in a row or column. Rows and columns must be unique. Tap to cycle symbols; long press to clear.</string>
    <string name="play_rules_nonogram">Numbers beside each row and above each column describe the lengths of filled runs in order. Leave at least one empty cell between runs. Use Fill or Cross to mark cells. Drag to paint, or long press to clear.</string>
    <string name="play_rules_minisudoku">Fill each row, column, and 2 by 3 box with digits 1 through 6 exactly once. Select a cell, then choose a digit. Notes toggles pencil marks; Erase clears the selected cell.</string>
    <string name="play_rules_sudoku">Fill each row, column, and 3 by 3 box with digits 1 through 9 exactly once. Select a cell, then choose a digit. Notes toggles pencil marks; Erase clears the selected cell.</string>
    <string name="play_rules_skyscrapers">Fill each row and column with building heights 1 to N exactly once. A number on an edge tells how many buildings you can see from that side; taller buildings hide shorter ones behind them. Select a cell, then choose a height. Notes toggles pencil marks.</string>
    <string name="play_rules_futoshiki">Fill each row and column with the digits 1 to N exactly once. The inequality sign between two neighbouring cells shows which digit must be smaller. Select a cell, then choose a digit. Notes toggles pencil marks.</string>
    <string name="play_rules_path">Join each equal-number pair with a path. Paths cannot branch, cross, or touch themselves, and every cell must be filled. Drag along empty cells to draw a path; each path joins the matching numbered endpoints.</string>
    <string name="play_rules_killersudoku">Fill each row, column, and 3 by 3 box with digits 1 through 9 exactly once. Digits inside each dashed cage must not repeat and must add up to the cage sum shown in its corner. Select a cell, then choose a digit. Notes toggles pencil marks; Erase clears the selected cell.</string>
    <string name="play_rules_arrows">Each cell holds one arrow or is empty. Tap an arrow to slide it off the board in its direction if every cell on its path is empty. Win when the board is empty. Tapping an arrow that cannot slide is a mistake and costs one life; three mistakes fail the level.</string>
    <string name="play_rules_coloursort">Pour from one tube onto another when the destination is empty or its top colour matches, and there is space. Win when every tube is empty or a single colour. If you get stuck, Continue adds one extra empty tube.</string>
    <string name="play_rules_mosaic">Each number is how many cells are filled in its 3 by 3 area (the cell and its neighbours). Fill or Cross cells until every clue is satisfied. Drag to paint, or long press to clear.</string>
    <string name="play_rules_klondike">Draw-1 Klondike. Build tableau down in alternating colours and foundations up in suit from ace to king. Tap a card, then tap a legal pile. If you get stuck, Continue grants one extra undo.</string>
    <string name="play_rules_tactics">Each puzzle has a unique mate. Tap a piece on your side, then tap the square it moves to. You play only the winning side; opponent replies are forced. A pawn that reaches the last rank becomes a queen.</string>
    <string name="tactics_cell_accessibility_label">Row %1$d, column %2$d, square %3$s, %4$s</string>
